<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="e90036cc">&lt;p&gt;
    The following documentation can assist in the successful preparation of an interview:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Interview introduction communication&lt;/strong&gt; - a communication that establishes an expectation that the
        interviewee will be contacted and also gives information about the engagement and what is required from them. This
        helps the client prepare for the interview, increasing the likelihood of productive client meetings, as well as
        develop client understanding of the engagement, reducing stakeholder uncertainty.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Interview log&lt;/strong&gt; - a list to facilitate a coordinated approach to arranging client interviews
        relating to the engagement. It is used to plan client interaction for effective client interviews. It supports a
        disciplined approach to coordinate meeting agendas and helps limit client disruption. The scheduling of client
        interviews provides milestones to keep the engagement on track and helps client personnel understand the required
        level of commitment and schedule their availability accordingly.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Interview agenda&lt;/strong&gt; - a list of key topics or objectives, along with key participant and the time and
        date.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
